{"title":"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Verifying_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Verifying Solutions</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For non-zero integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d31e8b160896cd96eacbab82bef727d6187be34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla y = x^{y} + 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c215099065b50ab7a436ec28342cdb60b8143682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\nabla 3 = 2^{3} + 4(2) = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"21\" />. Determine all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdd347f6609ef5118c8030f46e75e6108b754e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla 2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47c0c978f70d98a6d6a1ee6c47997f978e3d6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdd347f6609ef5118c8030f46e75e6108b754e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla 2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d446b18ef9844b27a83f6540d36842eb533db865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87eee93adaa4f84c003823c9e5a77f5d5099a4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x - 12 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dcadf6b880a738849845ef4a0bb57403e9898359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> while summing to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ace359e052dcb738584486ecd38c270f9641e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 6x - 2x - 12 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7af622378e55ed01dd90039c35afe240814d315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 6) - 2(x + 6) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/8575eb49185b2520f4432ed03a8facb81ec5aef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 2)(x + 6) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From this, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da133e03e1e46b894e416fc77ec35464fff163b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab67eabb9cda1ec96403faa3adc0a4f5ddfcc94f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 6 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> because their product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b124361978352af059e12c33e0b92950ae1c850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0ab473b3e1468a6df71c4858b283a1d6f4e66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = -6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"71\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47c0c978f70d98a6d6a1ee6c47997f978e3d6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdd347f6609ef5118c8030f46e75e6108b754e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla 2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d446b18ef9844b27a83f6540d36842eb533db865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab5b4802c0c3f460f731fa7cf2b43c78c212294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 4) = 12 = 2 \\times 6 = 2^{2} \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b124361978352af059e12c33e0b92950ae1c850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" /> works because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c2207a75b43ff2b80aa3717c3f91304e6bdf0bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c768058527b5b4d48df61c1a9147f1c5ddefb147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 6 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. However, we realize that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> increases, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c572e3cf69c353f11b1b8a7d2cb377434112e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> increases. This means that the other solution must be negative.\n</p><p>We also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab885591981ca08683a69bfd003cc89be75736f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c439b9dc606f5ca70f88a79d9f965c46a79ffdd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -6$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0ab473b3e1468a6df71c4858b283a1d6f4e66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = -6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"71\" height=\"26\" /> is also a solution.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Verifying_Solutions\">Verifying Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Verifying Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can check each solution. We also realize that we had a quadratic equation since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d446b18ef9844b27a83f6540d36842eb533db865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> is quadratic, so the number of distinct roots must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>First, we had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Using the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47c0c978f70d98a6d6a1ee6c47997f978e3d6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/18778266ae3e189238a045b58d3a70f454a2f58c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\nabla 2 = 2^{2} + 4(2) = 4 + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so it matches what we should have gotten.\n</p><p>Next, we had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c439b9dc606f5ca70f88a79d9f965c46a79ffdd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -6$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. Using the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47c0c978f70d98a6d6a1ee6c47997f978e3d6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\nabla y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0907c71c031213548ce658dacbc18c84f77f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6 \\nabla 2 = (-6)^{2} + 4(-6) = 36 - 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"270\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so it matches what we should have gotten.\n</p><p>This means that both of our answers for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> were correct.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC\">2021 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Individual 6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_7\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 7\">Individual 7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Individual 8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Individual 9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Individual 10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"